{"topic": "Gradient Descent and Learning Rate", "audience": "", "referenceMaterial": "[none provided]", "allowedTypes": {"chart": "Author a chart block for a LectureDoc lecture — a data chart (bar/line/area/scatter) rendered via Observable Plot, theme-aware. Reach for it whenever a page shows numeric comparison, trend over time, share/composition, or correlation — anything where seeing the shape of the numbers beats reading them. Prefer a chart over a table when magnitude/trend/relationship is the point; use a table only for exact nominal lookup where values are not being compared. Produces schema-valid chart block JSON.", "runnable": "Author a runnable (edit → Run) code cell block for a LectureDoc lecture — an in-browser Python (Pyodide) + JavaScript editor with a console and a result chart. Reach for it whenever the student should learn by writing/modifying and actually executing code themselves: implementing an algorithm by hand, tuning parameters and seeing the effect, exploratory what-if coding. Use a plain `code` block instead for read-only display the student will not run. Produces schema-valid runnable block JSON.", "hero": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "statement": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "pullquote": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "list": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "agenda": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "callout": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "formula": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "flow": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "table": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "code": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "compare": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "grid": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "timeline": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "freeform": "Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging. Produces schema-valid freeform block JSON.", "stats": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "diagram": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "graph": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "quiz": "Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Produces schema-valid quiz block JSON.", "sim": "Author a sim (simulation) block for a LectureDoc lecture — a parameter-driven interactive that recomputes and redraws in-browser as the student changes inputs. Reach for it whenever a quantitative or mechanistic process becomes clearer by letting the student turn a knob and watch the outcome change (physics/chem dynamics, algorithm behaviour, parameter sensitivity); pick a sim over a static chart when the interaction itself is the teaching point. Engines are chosen at build time: dynamics1d/searchCompare (declarative restricted-expression math → line charts), custom (sandboxed compute), widget (live canvas/SVG animation, geometric construction, or arbitrary mouse interaction). Skip it when the topic has no quantifiable/mechanistic process to manipulate — a sim with no real parameter to turn is decoration, not interaction. Produces schema-valid sim block JSON."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能复述本页核心结论", "keyClaim": "随机梯度下降：噪声反而能帮忙", "misconception": "", "visualTask": "视觉直接编码本页核心关系", "evidencePolicy": "none"}, "currentScene": {"id": "sgd-noise", "kind": "content", "eyebrow": "进阶技巧", "headline": "随机梯度下降：噪声反而能帮忙", "lead": "SGD 的梯度噪声有助于逃离局部极小，且计算效率更高。", "notes": "解释为什么实际中 SGD 比全批量更常用。", "blocks": [{"type": "list", "items": [{"lead": "计算效率", "text": "每次只用一个样本（或小批量）更新梯度，$O(1)$ 而非 $O(n)$，适合大规模数据。", "icon": "bar-chart-3"}, {"lead": "逃离局部极小", "text": "梯度噪声让参数有机会跳出浅的局部极小，找到更优解。", "icon": "plane"}, {"lead": "隐式正则化", "text": "随机采样引入的波动相当于一种正则项，提升泛化能力。", "icon": "camera"}], "id": "sgd-noise-r1"}, {"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
  .sgd-noise {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
    padding: 16px 20px 20px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    height: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .sgd-noise canvas {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 8px);
    cursor: crosshair;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 680 / 360;
  }
  .sgd-noise .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px 20px;
    padding: 4px 0 0;
  }
  .sgd-noise .ctrl-group {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sgd-noise label {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text2);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .sgd-noise input[type=range] {
    width: 80px;
    accent-color: var(--accent);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .sgd-noise .val {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
    min-width: 36px;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .sgd-noise button {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 12px;
    padding: 4px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius, 6px);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 150ms, border-color 150ms, transform 120ms;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .sgd-noise button:hover {
    background: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .sgd-noise button:active {
    transform: scale(0.96);
  }
  .sgd-noise .readout-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text2);
    padding: 2px 0 0;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .sgd-noise .readout-row .mono {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .sgd-noise .signature-tick {
    position: relative;
  }
  .sgd-noise .signature-tick::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--line);
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
</style>
<div class="sgd-noise">
  <canvas id="stage" width="680" height="360"></canvas>
  <div class="controls">
    <div class="ctrl-group">
      <label for="noiseScale">噪声幅度</label>
      <input type="range" id="noiseScale" min="0" max="0.5" step="0.01" value="0.3">
      <span class="val" id="noiseVal">0.30</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl-group">
      <label for="stepSize">步长</label>
      <input type="range" id="stepSize" min="0.01" max="0.2" step="0.005" value="0.08">
      <span class="val" id="stepVal">0.080</span>
    </div>
    <button id="toggle">⏸ 暂停</button>
    <button id="reset">↺ 重置</button>
  </div>
  <div class="readout-row">
    <span>位置 <span class="mono" id="posX">-1.50</span>, <span class="mono" id="posY">1.20</span></span>
    <span>轨迹点 <span class="mono" id="trailCount">5</span></span>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function() {
    const root = document.documentElement;
    const tok = (n) => getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
    const canvas = document.getElementById('stage');
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    const W = 680, H = 360;

    // state
    let paramX = -1.5;
    let paramY = 1.2;
    let noiseScale = 0.3;
    let stepSize = 0.08;
    let isRunning = true;
    let trail = [];

    // DOM refs
    const noiseSlider = document.getElementById('noiseScale');
    const noiseVal = document.getElementById('noiseVal');
    const stepSlider = document.getElementById('stepSize');
    const stepVal = document.getElementById('stepVal');
    const toggleBtn = document.getElementById('toggle');
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset');
    const posXEl = document.getElementById('posX');
    const posYEl = document.getElementById('posY');
    const trailCountEl = document.getElementById('trailCount');

    // loss landscape: double valley
    // f(x,y) = 0.5*(x+1.2)^2 + 0.3*(x-1.0)^2 + 0.8*y^2 + 0.2*sin(3*x)*cos(2*y)
    // local min near (-1.2, 0), global min near (1.0, 0)
    function lossGrad(x, y) {
      const gx = (x + 1.2) + 0.6 * (x - 1.0) + 0.6 * Math.cos(3 * x) * Math.cos(2 * y);
      const gy = 1.6 * y - 0.4 * Math.sin(3 * x) * Math.sin(2 * y);
      return { gx, gy };
    }

    // update: one step of SGD with noise
    function stepSGD() {
      if (!isRunning) return;
      const { gx, gy } = lossGrad(paramX, paramY);
      const noiseX = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
      const noiseY = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
      paramX -= stepSize * (gx + noiseX);
      paramY -= stepSize * (gy + noiseY);
      // clamp to range -2..2
      paramX = Math.min(2, Math.max(-2, paramX));
      paramY = Math.min(2, Math.max(-2, paramY));
      trail.push({ x: paramX, y: paramY });
      if (trail.length > 200) trail.shift();
    }

    // draw everything
    function draw() {
      const ink = tok('--ink');
      const accent = tok('--accent');
      const line = tok('--line');
      const text2 = tok('--text2');
      const bg = tok('--bg');
      const card = tok('--card');
      const dark = root.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'lab' || root.getAttribute('data-theme')?.includes('dark');

      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

      // map: x: -2..2 -> 60..620, y: -2..2 -> 300..60
      const mx = (x) => 60 + (x + 2) / 4 * 560;
      const my = (y) => 300 - (y + 2) / 4 * 240;

      // draw contour lines (schematic)
      ctx.strokeStyle = line;
      ctx.lineWidth = 0.8;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.25;
      for (let lev = 0.2; lev <= 2.0; lev += 0.3) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        let started = false;
        for (let px = -2; px <= 2; px += 0.04) {
          for (let py = -2; py <= 2; py += 0.04) {
            const v = 0.5 * (px + 1.2) ** 2 + 0.3 * (px - 1.0) ** 2 + 0.8 * py * py + 0.2 * Math.sin(3 * px) * Math.cos(2 * py);
            if (Math.abs(v - lev) < 0.08) {
              const sx = mx(px), sy = my(py);
              if (!started) { ctx.moveTo(sx, sy); started = true; }
              else ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
            }
          }
        }
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // mark local minima
      ctx.fillStyle = text2;
      ctx.font = '10px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.fillText('局部极小', mx(-1.2) - 20, my(0) - 8);
      ctx.fillText('全局极小', mx(1.0) - 20, my(0) - 8);
      ctx.fillStyle = text2;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.4;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(mx(-1.2), my(0), 4, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fill();
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(mx(1.0), my(0), 4, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fill();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // draw trail
      if (trail.length > 1) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = accent;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;
        ctx.globalAlpha = 0.5;
        if (dark) {
          ctx.shadowColor = accent;
          ctx.shadowBlur = 6;
        }
        ctx.beginPath();
        for (let i = 0; i < trail.length; i++) {
          const sx = mx(trail[i].x), sy = my(trail[i].y);
          if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(sx, sy);
          else ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
        }
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.shadowBlur = 0;
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;
      }

      // draw current point
      const cx = mx(paramX), cy = my(paramY);
      ctx.fillStyle = accent;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(cx, cy, 6, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = card;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.stroke();

      // draw crosshair signature (lab theme)
      ctx.strokeStyle = text2;
      ctx.lineWidth = 0.8;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.3;
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx - 14, cy); ctx.lineTo(cx + 14, cy); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx, cy - 14); ctx.lineTo(cx, cy + 14); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // corner mono readout (signature)
      ctx.fillStyle = text2;
      ctx.font = '10px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.fillText('x ' + paramX.toFixed(3) + '  y ' + paramY.toFixed(3), 12, 20);
      ctx.fillText('步 ' + stepSize.toFixed(3) + ' 噪 ' + noiseScale.toFixed(2), 12, 34);

      // update DOM readouts
      posXEl.textContent = paramX.toFixed(2);
      posYEl.textContent = paramY.toFixed(2);
      trailCountEl.textContent = trail.length;
    }

    // main loop
    let lastTime = performance.now();
    function loop(now) {
      const dt = Math.min((now - lastTime) / 1000, 0.03);
      lastTime = now;
      // run multiple steps per frame for visible motion
      if (isRunning) {
        const stepsPerFrame = 2;
        for (let i = 0; i < stepsPerFrame; i++) stepSGD();
      }
      draw();
      requestAnimationFrame(loop);
    }

    // interactions
    noiseSlider.addEventListener('input', () => {
      noiseScale = parseFloat(noiseSlider.value);
      noiseVal.textContent = noiseScale.toFixed(2);
    });
    stepSlider.addEventListener('input', () => {
      stepSize = parseFloat(stepSlider.value);
      stepVal.textContent = stepSize.toFixed(3);
    });
    toggleBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      isRunning = !isRunning;
      toggleBtn.textContent = isRunning ? '⏸ 暂停' : '▶ 继续';
    });
    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      paramX = -1.5;
      paramY = 1.2;
      trail = [];
      // re-initialize with 5 trail points toward local min
      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        const t = (i + 1) / 6;
        trail.push({ x: -1.5 + t * 0.3, y: 1.2 - t * 0.8 });
      }
      paramX = -1.2;
      paramY = 0.4;
      if (!isRunning) {
        isRunning = true;
        toggleBtn.textContent = '⏸ 暂停';
      }
    });

    // initial trail: 5 points from start toward local min
    trail = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
      const t = (i + 1) / 6;
      trail.push({ x: -1.5 + t * 0.3, y: 1.2 - t * 0.8 });
    }
    paramX = -1.2;
    paramY = 0.4;

    // start
    requestAnimationFrame(loop);
  })();
